    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d75-a1">

                <pb facs="0132" n="125" xml:id="pg125"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 75.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Commander O’Neil to
                        Mr. Herbert.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Cablegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Limon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-07-17"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>For the protection of American interests another man-of-war required. Affairs are
                    very disturbed at Bluefields. There are no prospects of a settlement. The
                    situation is alarming. It is feared that hostilities can not be avoided. The <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Marblehead</hi> is protecting American interests at
                    Bluefields. The only means of telegraphing is from Port Limon, Costa Rica, by
                    schooner.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
